    "done_when": "Done when. A test gives a row whose stream exists and reads back on it the same two figures the routing derivation computes from that stream. A second test gives a row whose stream is gone, reads both figures recorded absent rather than zero, and reads that retention then treats the directory as reapable. A negative control that skips the write leaves retention withholding the same directory. Before any live row is written, an independent on-disk census on all_debug counts, per project, the withheld rows whose run directory holds a stream file and those whose run directory holds none. After the fill, the per-project count of rows recorded absent equals that census's no-stream count exactly, and the filled-plus-unmeasurable count equals its stream-present count; a run that records more absences than the census found has failed, whatever retention reports afterwards. Five filled rows per project, chosen at random, are re-derived from their streams and match the recorded figures. A retention dry run on all_debug from a fresh cursor then reports a missing-derived-figure count of zero. Each project's ledger commit names only ledger paths. The gate runs on all_debug and its log is written to the section's evidence fragment.",
